foundation.question_text:
A rectangle is cut along its diagonal. How many pieces are made, and what shape is each piece?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4,2.4);
\coordinate (D) at (0,2.4);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (A)--(C);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
The diagonal divides the rectangle into two pieces.
Each piece is a right-angled triangle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,2.4);\coordinate (D) at (0,2.4);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;\draw[thick] (A)--(C);\node at (2.8,0.7) {$1$};\node at (1.2,1.7) {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
A triangular piece is cut from the left of this parallelogram. To which side should it be translated to form a rectangle?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (5.7,2.4);
\coordinate (D) at (1.2,2.4);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (D)--(1.2,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two matching right-angled triangles are shown. Which movement can join the second triangle to the first to make a rectangle?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.4,0)--(0,1.6)--cycle;
\draw (4.6,0)--(2.2,1.6)--(4.6,1.6)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
The second triangle already has the complementary orientation. Slide it left until the sloping sides meet.
Translate it to the left.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (2.4,0);\coordinate (C) at (2.4,1.6);\coordinate (D) at (0,1.6);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;\draw[dashed] (A)--(C);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

