development.question_text:
Sofia cuts a parallelogram along the dashed height and moves the left triangle to the right. What simple shape will be formed?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6.4,2.7);
\coordinate (D) at (1.4,2.7);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (D)--(1.4,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A triangle is duplicated. Describe how the copy can be moved so the pair forms a parallelogram.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[fill=gray!20] (0,0)--(3.4,0)--(1.1,2.2)--cycle;
\draw (5,0)--(8.4,0)--(6.1,2.2)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
Rotate the copy through $180^{\circ}$, then translate it until a matching side joins the first triangle.
The outer boundary is a parallelogram.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (3.4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4.5,2.2);\coordinate (D) at (1.1,2.2);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;\draw[dashed] (A)--(C);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A rectangle is divided by both diagonals. How many triangular pieces are produced?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.6,2.8);
\coordinate (D) at (0,2.8);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (A)--(C);
\draw[dashed] (B)--(D);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
The two diagonals cross once and divide the rectangle into one triangular region beside each side.
$4$ triangular pieces
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4.6,0);\coordinate (C) at (4.6,2.8);\coordinate (D) at (0,2.8);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;\draw[thick] (A)--(C);\draw[thick] (B)--(D);\node at (2.3,0.55) {$1$};\node at (3.55,1.4) {$2$};\node at (2.3,2.25) {$3$};\node at (1.05,1.4) {$4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

